---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Stack from "../components/Stack.astro";
import { site, research } from "../data/site";
import { papers } from "../data/papers";
import { education, theses } from "../data/education";
import { aboutJsonLd } from "../data/identity";
import { volunteering } from "../data/speaking";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Abi Aryan: AI Infrastructure Engineer, Joule founder, Maven instructor, Invited Expert and Faculty Member on AI Inferencing at Andreessen Horowitz Academy. Doctoral research in HPC distributed systems. Master's theses at NOVA IMS and LSE. The stack I teach: vLLM, SGLang, KV cache, CUDA, Kubernetes."
  jsonLd={aboutJsonLd}
>
  <section class="about-split">
    <div class="about-copy">
    <p class="label">About</p>
    <h1>Abi Aryan</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I am an <span class="skim">AI Infrastructure Engineer</span> building inference systems for data centers,
      neoclouds, and hyperscalers. I founded
      <a href={site.links.joule}>Joule</a>, an inference power economics engine that
      connects physical GPU energy to token throughput and SLO goodput.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I have spent over a decade building production ML systems and now work across the
      inference stack, from
      <span class="skim">performance-critical runtimes and distributed systems to GPUs,
      compilers, and cluster efficiency</span>. I architect infrastructure for serving systems
      built on inference engines such as TensorRT-LLM, TorchDynamo, SGLang, and vLLM.
    </p>
    <p>
      My focus is not maintaining these engines, but making
      <span class="skim">high-concurrency serving</span>
      intelligible and reliable at scale, across the entire infrastructure path: from the
      client and request layer, through
      <span class="skim">tokens, bytes, GPUs, and network fabric</span>, all the
      way to
      <span class="skim">data-center capacity planning, power, and cooling</span>.
    </p>
    <p>
      In other words, I care about the complete path from a request to the orchestrators
      down to the physical resources that produce it:
      <span class="skim">the tokens generated, the bytes moved, the energy consumed, the heat that ultimately has to be removed, and data-center capacity planning</span>.
    </p>
    <p>
      At <a href={site.links.joule}>Joule</a>, I work on the infra engineering that
      manages the <span class="skim">economics of inference power</span>: connecting GPU energy consumption to token
      throughput and SLO goodput, so cluster operators and fleet managers can understand
      the cost and physical reality of inference alongside its performance.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am a <span class="skim">doctoral researcher in HPC distributed systems</span>, studying SLO-aware
      inference optimization and hardware-aware compiler design for supercomputers. As part
      of this research, I am developing a <span class="skim">digital twin for LLM inference</span>
      that lets operators manage energy while protecting latency SLOs.
    </p>
    <p>
      I build the systems, measure them, research them, write about them, and teach them.
      I am an <span class="skim">Invited Expert and Faculty Member on AI Inferencing</span> for
      <a href={site.links.academy}>Andreessen Horowitz Academy (The Academy SF)</a>, and I
      teach masterclasses on Maven, including
      <a href={site.links.maven}>AI Inference Engineering &amp; Systems Design</a>
      for mid-to-senior engineers and
      <a href={site.links.mavenIntro}>AI Inference for FDE and PM Roles</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am the author of
      <a href={site.links.llmops}>LLMOps</a>
      (written 2023-2024, completed December 2024, published in 2025), now translated into
      Korean, Japanese, Russian, and Simplified Chinese. I also wrote
      <a href={site.links.llmopsWhat}>What is LLMOps</a> (O'Reilly, 2024). My next book,
      <a href="/books/">GPU Engineering: AI Inference and System Design</a> (Packt), is
      nearing completion, with publication planned for late 2026 or early 2027. I write
      <a href={site.links.modelcraft}>ModelCraft</a> and review for NeurIPS, ACL, EMNLP,
      ICML, ICLR, TMLR, and AABI.
    </p>
    <p>
      Previously, I co-founded <a href={site.links.abide}>Abide</a>, a research lab focused
      on reflective intelligence and neuro-symbolic models for agents, where I mainly
      contributed to building platform and observability solutions for agentic reasoning
      in LLMs. That work was presented at NeurIPS 2025. Abide is prior work, whereas
      <a href={site.links.joule}>Joule</a> is the company I run today.
    </p>
    <p>
      A mathematician by training, I was a visiting research scholar at
      <span class="skim">UCLA's Cognitive Systems Lab</span> from 2018-19 under Dr.
      <a href={site.links.pearl}>Judea Pearl</a>, the 2012 recipient of the ACM A.M. Turing
      Award. There I worked on intelligence in agents, with research spanning causal
      inference, AutoML, and multi-agent learning.
    </p>
    <p>
      For talks, see <a href="/speaking/">Speaking</a>. For the audit and advisory work,
      see <a href="/advisory/">Advisory</a>.
    </p>
    </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-aside">
      <Stack />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Doctoral work</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom: 1.6rem">{site.doctorate.statement}</p>
    <div class="grid-3">
      {
        research.map((item) => (
          <article class="card">
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.note}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Education</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="list">
      {
        education.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <span class="meta">{item.year}</span>
            <div>
              {item.href ? (
                <a class="title" href={item.href}>{item.title}</a>
              ) : (
                <span class="title">{item.title}</span>
              )}
              <p class="note">{item.note}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Theses</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="list">
      {
        theses.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <span class="meta">{item.year}</span>
            <div>
              {item.href ? (
                <a class="title" href={item.href}>{item.title}</a>
              ) : (
                <span class="title">{item.title}</span>
              )}
              <p class="note">{item.note}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Papers</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="list">
      {
        papers.map((item) => (
          <li>
            <span class="meta">{item.year}</span>
            <div>
              {item.href ? (
                <a class="title" href={item.href}>{item.title}</a>
              ) : (
                <span class="title">{item.title}</span>
              )}
              <p class="note">{item.note}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <details class="year" open>
      <summary>Reviewing and service</summary>
      {
        volunteering.map((item) => (
          <div class="talk">
            <div class="when">{item.when}</div>
            <div>
              {item.href ? <a href={item.href}>{item.what}</a> : item.what}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="section media-block">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Media</h2>
      <span class="label">October 2024</span>
    </div>
    <video class="media-clip" controls playsinline preload="metadata">
      <source src="/assets/billboard.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
    </video>
    <p>I was featured on the Times Square Billboard by <a href={site.links.topmate}>Topmate</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
